"""Original incident response and recovery scenarios."""
ITEMS=[]
def group(o,rows):
 for k,(s,e) in enumerate(rows):ITEMS.append((s,[o[k]]+[v for j,v in enumerate(o) if j!=k],e))
group(['Prepare response capabilities','Analyze the reported event','Contain the confirmed incident','Improve after the incident'],[
('Before an incident, a team verifies contact lists, responsibilities, tools and escalation paths. Which response activity is being performed?', 'Preparation establishes the capabilities needed to respond effectively.'),
('An unusual account alert arrives. Responders examine available evidence to determine what happened and whether an incident exists. Which activity is this?', 'Analysis interprets the event and establishes its nature and scope.'),
('A confirmed compromised workstation is restricted from communicating with other production systems under the approved response plan. Which activity is this?', 'Containment limits ongoing damage and spread while supporting further response.'),
('After recovery, a team documents why escalation failed and changes the procedure to prevent recurrence. Which activity is this?', 'Post-incident improvement uses lessons to strengthen future prevention and response.')])
group(['Remove the established cause','Restore the trusted service','Monitor the recovered environment','Communicate the incident status'],[
('Responders have contained an intrusion and identified the persistence mechanism. Which activity eliminates that mechanism before return to service?', 'Eradication removes the established malicious cause and persistence, rather than merely reconnecting the service.'),
('A cleaned system and verified backup are ready, and the recovery owner authorizes re-establishing the business function. Which activity follows?', 'Restoration returns a trusted service to operation under the recovery plan.'),
('A recovered service is operating again. Responders now look for recurrence or unexpected residual behavior. Which activity is being performed?', 'Post-restoration monitoring helps identify incomplete recovery or renewed compromise.'),
('The approved response lead must give affected business teams a factual update on scope, service impact and next steps. Which activity is this?', 'Status communication coordinates stakeholders using verified information and the agreed channel.')])
group(['Preserve the original evidence','Record the custody transfer','Obtain the required authority','Document the analytical method'],[
('An analyst is about to work on the only copy of a potentially relevant storage image. What evidentiary safeguard is needed before analysis changes it?', 'Preserve the original and work on controlled copies as appropriate so the source evidence remains available.'),
('An evidence drive passes from the collecting technician to the forensic examiner. Which record preserves traceability of that handoff?', 'Record who transferred and received the evidence, when, and under what handling conditions.'),
('A proposed examination includes privately owned devices beyond the current authorization. Which issue must be resolved before expanding the examination?', 'Confirm legal and organizational authority for the additional scope rather than assuming access permission.'),
('An examiner reaches a conclusion from several tools and transformations. What record allows another qualified examiner to assess how the conclusion was reached?', 'Document methods, tool details, assumptions and relevant results so the analysis can be evaluated.')])
group(['Capture volatile evidence','Acquire persistent evidence','Verify an evidence copy','Build the incident timeline'],[
('An authorized examiner needs the current running-process and memory state that will disappear when the host powers off. Which evidence activity addresses that need?', 'Capture relevant volatile evidence using an approved method before it disappears, while recording any changes caused by collection.'),
('A case requires a controlled copy of stored files and file-system metadata for later examination. Which evidence activity is appropriate?', 'Acquire persistent storage evidence using approved procedures that preserve relevant information.'),
('A collected image is transferred to another analysis system. The examiner compares a suitable cryptographic digest with the recorded acquisition digest. What is the purpose?', 'The comparison checks that the copied evidence matches the recorded image; it does not prove every fact about its original source.'),
('Responders need to order the validated login, process and transfer events to understand the sequence of compromise. Which analysis product serves this need?', 'An incident timeline combines supported events and time assumptions into an ordered account.')])
group(['Recovery time objective','Recovery point objective','Maximum tolerable downtime','Backup retention period'],[
('A service plan sets a target of restoring a business function within four hours after disruption. Which measure is this?', 'The recovery time objective is the targeted restoration interval.'),
('A business can tolerate losing no more than the last 15 minutes of committed records following recovery. Which measure expresses that tolerance?', 'The recovery point objective expresses the tolerated data-loss interval measured back from the disruption.'),
('A business impact analysis identifies the longest interruption the organization can tolerate before consequences become unacceptable. Which measure is this?', 'Maximum tolerable downtime describes the outer business tolerance, which should inform shorter recovery targets.'),
('A policy requires weekly backup copies to remain available for six months before approved expiration. Which measure is being specified?', 'Retention specifies how long backup copies are kept, not how quickly service must be restored.')])
group(['A full backup','An incremental backup','A differential backup','A tested restoration'],[
('A backup captures all data within the selected scope regardless of previous backup changes. Which approach is this?', 'A full backup copies the whole selected scope.'),
('A backup captures changes since the most recent backup in the sequence, whether that previous backup was full or incremental. Which approach is this?', 'Incremental backup captures changes since the preceding backup; restoration may require the complete relevant chain.'),
('A backup captures all changes since the last full backup, even if some were captured yesterday. Which approach is this?', 'Differential backup accumulates changes since the full baseline.'),
('Operators use a retained copy to rebuild an isolated service and verify its required data and functionality. What has been performed?', 'A restoration test checks recoverability and function; merely completing a backup job does not do this.')])
group(['An isolated recovery copy','Geographic recovery separation','Redundant live capacity','A documented failback procedure'],[
('A ransomware incident could reach both production and continuously writable backup storage through the same credentials. Which recovery design feature addresses that shared compromise path?', 'An appropriately isolated copy reduces the chance that the same compromised access can alter all recovery data.'),
('Primary and recovery facilities sit in the same flood zone. Which design feature addresses that correlated physical hazard?', 'Geographic separation should account for shared hazards and dependencies, not just a different street address.'),
('A service must continue operating when a single server fails, without waiting for a full rebuild. Which feature addresses immediate capacity continuity?', 'Redundant live capacity supports continuity after a component failure, subject to correct failover design.'),
('A service operates at an alternate site after recovery. Staff need an approved way to return to the normal site without losing new records. Which procedure is required?', 'Failback planning coordinates return, synchronization and validation after alternate operation.')])
group(['A plan walkthrough','A tabletop exercise','A technical restoration exercise','A controlled failover exercise'],[
('Participants read a recovery plan together to confirm contact details and responsibilities without introducing an incident scenario. Which activity is this?', 'A walkthrough checks the documented plan and roles through structured review.'),
('Participants discuss decisions and escalation during a simulated outage, without moving live workloads. Which exercise is this?', 'A tabletop uses a scenario to practice coordination and decision-making without executing a live recovery.'),
('Technicians rebuild an isolated application from retained backup data and test its functions. Which exercise is this?', 'A technical restoration exercise verifies the ability to reconstruct and use the service from recovery material.'),
('Under an approved test plan, a service transfers actual processing to its alternate environment and validates continuity. Which exercise is this?', 'Controlled failover tests the operational transition to alternate capacity, with appropriate risk controls.')])
group(['The RTO is met; the RPO is met','The RTO is met; the RPO is missed','The RTO is missed; the RPO is met','The RTO is missed; the RPO is missed'],[
('A service has a four-hour RTO and a 30-minute RPO. It is restored in three hours with 20 minutes of lost records. Which assessment is correct?', 'Three hours is within four, and 20 minutes is within 30, so both targets are met.'),
('A billing service has a two-hour RTO and a ten-minute RPO. Recovery takes 90 minutes, but 25 minutes of transactions are lost. Which assessment is correct?', 'Restoration is within two hours, but data loss exceeds ten minutes.'),
('A warehouse system has a one-hour RTO and a 15-minute RPO. Recovery takes 80 minutes and loses five minutes of updates. Which assessment is correct?', 'The 80-minute restoration exceeds the one-hour RTO, while five minutes of loss is within the RPO.'),
('A booking service has a three-hour RTO and a five-minute RPO. Recovery takes four hours and loses 12 minutes of bookings. Which assessment is correct?', 'Both the restoration interval and the data-loss interval exceed their respective targets.')])
assert len(ITEMS)==36
